# shell: desktop
# work: home
# mkdir: /dev/shm/.Trash
# file: /dev/shm/.Trash/planted.txt hi
# PVN-027: the Trash window is the union over every volume's trash, kept
# live -- a move into ANY trash appears there on the refresh beat.
wait 10
note trash a.txt, answering the question, then open the Trash
click-row 1
wait 2
key Delete
wait 5
key m
wait 30
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/.Trash/a.txt
click 170 30
wait 2
click 170 30
wait 8
expect-windows 2
note TWO rows: the file just trashed here, and the one another volume's
note trash already held -- the union, not the folder
expect-rows 2
note a second file trashed while the window is open joins the union live
key w ctrl
wait 3
click-row 1
wait 2
key Delete
wait 5
key m
wait 30
click 170 30
wait 2
click 170 30
wait 8
expect-rows 3
quit
